    {
      "title": "Reduce directly toward gradient owners",
      "explanation": "Reduce-scatter combines the local contributions and routes only the relevant reduced shard to each owner. The output bank changes from unavailable to $g_A,g_B$: $g_A$ belongs with $p_A$, while $g_B$ belongs with $p_B$. Unlike an all-reduce, this operation does not leave every process holding the complete reduced gradient.",
